# WHITELIST approach: exclude EVERYTHING by default, then re-include (!) only
# the exact files the extension needs at runtime. Anything new added to the
# repo is automatically excluded from the VSIX, so dev notes, local plans and
# build intermediates can never ship by accident.
#
# vsce quirk: negated (!) patterns always win, regardless of line order.
# So we whitelist exact FILES (not folders with **), otherwise things like
# *.map inside whitelisted folders can't be excluded anymore.
#
# package.json and extension.vsixmanifest are always packaged automatically.
# If the build ever emits a NEW runtime file, it must be added here explicitly.

# 1) exclude everything
**

# 2) re-include the exact runtime files
!readme.md
!LICENSE
!CHANGELOG.md
!out/extension.js
!media/webview.js
!media/webview.css
!media/hljs-dark.css
!media/hljs-light.css
!resources/icon.png
!resources/waypoint-dark.svg
!resources/waypoint-light.svg
# The agent kit that "Install skills" copies into other repos. build.ts wipes
# and regenerates this dir from .claude/ and .agents/ (waypoint* only) on
# every build, and only its .md files and .py helpers (tick.py) are
# re-included — a stray file of any other type in the folder still can't ship.
!resources/kit/**/*.md
!resources/kit/**/*.py
